{title: What is left of the night}
{subtitle: Isaiah 21:11–17}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 80}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Bb] | [Dm] |
| [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm]Someone calls out from [Bb]Seir
[Dm]Watchman how far has the night [Bb]gone?
[Gm]He answers morning is [Dm]coming
But [C]night remains on the ho[Dm]rizon
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
What is left of the [Gm]night
[C]If you must ask then [F]ask
[Bb]Come back again to [Gm]seek
[A]What is left of the [Dm]night [Bb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dm]Caravans of Dedan [Bb]stop
[Dm]Camp in the thickets of Ara[Bb]bia
[Gm]People of Tema bring [Dm]water
[C]Meet the fugitives with [Dm]bread
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
What is left of the [Gm]night
[C]If you must ask then [F]ask
[Bb]Come back again to [Gm]seek
[A]What is left of the [Dm]night
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb]They flee from the [Dm]drawn sword
[Bb]From the bent bow and [Dm]battle
[Bb]The Lord says in one [Dm]year
[C]The splendor of Kedar [Dm]ends
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Bb]The remnant of the bow[Dm]men
[Bb]Warriors of Kedar will be [Dm]few
[Bb]The God of Israel [Dm]has spoken
[C]His word stands firm and [Dm]true
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
What is left of the [Gm]night [C][F][Bb][Gm][A][Dm][Gm][A]
Come back again to seek [Dm]
{end_of_verse}
